        <div class="subhead">Botanical database · floristic, climatic & taxonomic management</div>

        <p><strong>Alamut</strong> is a comprehensive botanical database management system designed for floristic research, climatic data analysis, and taxonomic organization. Named after the historic mountain fortress, this application provides a robust platform for managing complex botanical datasets with an emphasis on scientific accuracy and data relationships.</p>

        <h2>Core Features</h2>
            <div class="grid-2">
                <div class="card-soft">
                <h4 style="margin-top:0;">Taxonomic Management</h4>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom:0;">
                    <li>Complete hierarchy from APG Groups to Species</li>
                    <li>Synonyms, accepted names, conservation status</li>
                    <li>Infraspecific ranks (subspecies, varieties, forms)</li>
                    <li>Author citations and protologue information</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card-soft">
                <h4 style="margin-top:0;">Dataset Types</h4>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom:0;">
                    <li><span class="badge">FL</span> Floristic (species presence/absence)</li>
                    <li><span class="badge">CN</span> Chorological (geographic distribution)</li>
                    <li><span class="badge">LM</span> Lifeform / Morphological</li>
                    <li><span class="badge">ST</span> Station / Climatic (T & P)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card-soft">
                <h4 style="margin-top:0;">Geographic Organization</h4>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom:0;">
                    <li>Countries → Provinces → Stations</li>
                    <li>Coordinate systems for mapping</li>
                    <li>Altitude ranges & climatic data</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card-soft">
                <h4 style="margin-top:0;">Notes System</h4>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom:0;">
                    <li>Universal notes for any entity</li>
                    <li>Todo items with due dates</li>
                    <li>Bookmarking & sharing</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

        <h2>User Account System</h2>
        <p>When you create an account, you'll have access to features based on your user tags:</p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="tag-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Tag</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">1</span> Active</td><td>Standard active user</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">2</span> AdminAccount</td><td>Full administrative privileges</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">4</span> GoldAccount</td><td>Premium features access</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">8</span> SilverAccount</td><td>Extended feature set</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">16</span> RemindDueNotes</td><td>Automatic reminders for pending todos</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">32</span> DueNotesDays</td><td>Configure reminder timing (default: 7 days)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">64</span> CanChangeNickname</td><td>Ability to modify display name</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">128</span> OnExpire</td><td>Account behavior when subscription ends</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><span class="tag-pill">256</span> UseFaCalendar</td><td>Persian calendar support</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

        <h2>Working with Data</h2>

        <h3>1. Navigating the Taxonomic Tree</h3>
        <p><strong>APG Groups</strong> (Angiosperm Phylogeny Group):</p>
            <ul>
            <li><span class="mono">6'000</span> – Angiosperms (main group)</li>
            <li><span class="mono">6'400</span> – Eudicots</li>
            <li><span class="mono">6'620</span> – Rosids</li>
            <li><span class="mono">6'660</span> – Asterids</li>
            <li><span class="mono">10'000</span> – RESERVED (future classification)</li>
            </ul>
        <p><strong>Hierarchy flow:</strong> <span class="highlight">APG Group</span> → Order → Family → Genus → Species → Infraspecific ranks</p>

        <h3>2. Managing Datasets</h3>
        <h4>Creating a dataset</h4>
            <ol>
            <li>Select dataset type (FL, CN, LM, or ST)</li>
            <li>Provide abbreviation and full name</li>
            <li>Add reference (publication year, language)</li>
            <li>Specify geographical location (Province)</li>
            <li>Input environmental data: coordinates, altitude (max/min/avg), temperature, precipitation</li>
            </ol>
        <h4>Adding records</h4>
            <ul>
            <li><strong>FL</strong> – link species with infraspecific info</li>
            <li><strong>CN</strong> – connect species with geographic linestring</li>
            <li><strong>LM</strong> – link species with lifeform/morphological traits</li>
            <li><strong>ST</strong> – add climate station data with monthly readings</li>
            </ul>

        <h3>3. Working with Notes</h3>
        <p>The note system is versatile and can be attached to: APG Groups, Orders, Families, Genera, Species, Datasets, Stations, Sets, Users.</p>
            <ul>
            <li>Mark as <strong>Todo</strong> with due dates</li>
            <li>Track completion status</li>
            <li>Set importance with bookmarks</li>
            <li>Share with other users</li>
            </ul>

        <h3>4. Sets and Grouping</h3>
        <p><strong>Sets</strong> allow you to organize data into collections:</p>
            <ul>
            <li><strong>Floristic Sets</strong> – group related floristic datasets</li>
            <li><strong>Climatic Sets</strong> – organize climatic data for comparison</li>
            </ul>

        <h2>💡 Tips for Effective Use</h2>
            <div class="grid-2">
                <div class="card-soft">
                <h4 style="margin-top:0;">📌 Best Practices</h4>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom:0;">
                    <li><strong>Taxonomic accuracy</strong> – verify species IDs (WFO), accepted names, document status</li>
                    <li><strong>Data quality</strong> – fill all available fields, use consistent naming, add references</li>
                    <li><strong>Geographic precision</strong> – include coordinates, altitude ranges, link to provinces</li>
                    <li><strong>Note management</strong> – create todos for verification, use due dates, share notes</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="card-soft">
                <h4 style="margin-top:0;">⚡ Quick Actions</h4>
                    <ul style="margin-bottom:0;">
                    <li><span class="tag-pill">4</span> Bookmark important species</li>
                    <li><span class="tag-pill">8</span> Mark Todo items for follow-up</li>
                    <li><span class="tag-pill">16</span> Flag as Read to review records</li>
                    <li><span class="tag-pill">32</span> Complete tasks to track progress</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

